        "date": "2026-11-16T14:13:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gate): keep the quick build step when one fn step does not cover the build list\n\nThe quick plan skipped the crate build step when the crate had exactly one\nrun step. A second binary that had only changed heavy-lane fns was then in\nthe build list but no step compiled it. Now the build step is skipped only\nwhen the one run step covers the one target of the build list.\n\nAlso from the review of PR #1952:\n- batch stops after a failed whole-gate build, as release does;\n- a dry run does not read the checkout for each step;\n- xtask/src/quick.rs is under 400 lines again.\n\nPinned by tests::heavy_fn_in_a_second_binary_keeps_the_build_step and the\nbatch case in lanes_tests::release_executor_overlaps_lanes_and_keeps_failure_and_checkout_guards.\n\nRefs #1941\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
